@startuml
title Modelo 2D — mesmos módulos e ponto de entrada
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "executável" {
  class "main.cpp" as Main
  class "rheo::RheoLBMApp" as App
  class "RunShallowWaterLbm2DApp()" as Run2D
}
package domain {
  class ShallowWaterSettings
  enum ShallowWaterScenario
  class ShallowWaterSnapshot
}
package simulation {
  class ShallowWaterLbm2DSolver
  class ShallowWaterSession
}
package application {
  class ShallowWaterController
}
package renderer {
  class ShallowWaterRenderer
  interface IOverlayPass
}
package ui {
  class ShallowWaterInterface
  class ImGuiLayer
}
package "graphics / platform / events\ncompartilhados" as Infrastructure

Main --> App : --model 2d
App --> Run2D : Run()
Run2D ..> ShallowWaterController
Run2D ..> ShallowWaterRenderer
Run2D ..> ShallowWaterInterface
Run2D --> Infrastructure
ShallowWaterController *-- ShallowWaterSession
ShallowWaterSession *-- ShallowWaterLbm2DSolver
ShallowWaterLbm2DSolver --> ShallowWaterSettings
ShallowWaterLbm2DSolver --> ShallowWaterSnapshot
ShallowWaterController --> ShallowWaterScenario
ShallowWaterInterface --> ShallowWaterController : seleção e execução
ShallowWaterInterface *-- ImGuiLayer
ShallowWaterInterface ..|> IOverlayPass
ShallowWaterInterface --> ShallowWaterRenderer : campos e opções do mapa
ShallowWaterRenderer --> ShallowWaterSnapshot : leitura
ShallowWaterRenderer --> Infrastructure : frame Vulkan
ShallowWaterRenderer --> IOverlayPass : desenho

note bottom of Main
  src/main.cpp é único.
  Os dois modelos são compilados no mesmo executável.
  --model 2d seleciona este fluxo; o padrão é 3D.
  Somente o fluxo selecionado cria janela, Vulkan e ImGui.
  Os controllers continuam separados.
  Os módulos agregam as dependências dos dois modelos;
  o solver de águas rasas continua executando na CPU.
end note
@enduml
